<title>INDIA: India soybean, meal steady, oil down.</title>
<headline>India soybean, meal steady, oil down.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in central Indian markets in limited trading on Tuesday as arrivals were poor, dealers said. Business volume was dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil solvent was down 100 rupees per tonne on limited demand from vanaspati units and refineries. Soyoil refined was up by 200 rupees per tonne on good demand in local market. Business was good and the undertone was mixed.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices remained steady in very thin trading. Soymeal yellow was $322 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) in bulk for west coast Indian ports in export. Rapeseed extraction was $120-121 per tonne in export and was 4,300 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. Business volume was dull and the undertone was strong.</p>
